(Introduction to Photosynthesis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Photosynthesis is the process by which green plants, algae, and some bacteria convert) Tj
T*
(light energy, usually from the sun, into chemical energy stored in glucose. This process) Tj
T*
(sustains nearly all life on Earth by producing the oxygen we breathe and the organic) Tj
T*
(compounds that form the base of most food chains.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Overall Equation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The overall chemical equation for photosynthesis is: six molecules of carbon dioxide plus) Tj
T*
(six molecules of water, in the presence of light energy, yield one molecule of glucose) Tj
T*
(plus six molecules of oxygen. In short: 6 CO2 + 6 H2O + light -> C6H12O6 + 6 O2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The Two Main Stages) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Photosynthesis occurs in two linked stages inside the chloroplast. The light-dependent) Tj
T*
(reactions take place in the thylakoid membrane, where chlorophyll absorbs sunlight and) Tj
T*
(uses that energy to split water molecules, releasing oxygen and producing ATP and NADPH.) Tj
T*
(The light-independent reactions, also called the Calvin cycle, take place in the stroma.) Tj
T*
(They use the ATP and NADPH from the first stage to fix carbon dioxide into glucose.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why Chlorophyll Matters) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Chlorophyll is the green pigment found in chloroplasts. It absorbs mostly red and blue) Tj
T*
(wavelengths of light while reflecting green light, which is why most plant leaves appear) Tj
T*
(green. Without chlorophyll, plants could not capture the light energy needed to drive the) Tj
T*
(light-dependent reactions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Factors That Affect the Rate of Photosynthesis) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Several environmental factors influence how quickly a plant photosynthesizes: light) Tj
T*
(intensity, carbon dioxide concentration, and temperature. Increasing light intensity or) Tj
T*
(carbon dioxide concentration generally increases the rate of photosynthesis up to a point,) Tj
T*
(after which some other factor becomes limiting. Extreme temperatures can denature the) Tj
T*
(enzymes involved in the Calvin cycle, slowing the process down.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Why Photosynthesis Matters) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Photosynthesis is the foundation of nearly every food chain on Earth. It also regulates) Tj
T*
(atmospheric oxygen and carbon dioxide levels, making it essential to the planet's climate) Tj
T*
(and to the survival of aerobic organisms, including humans.) Tj
ET
